From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 14:01:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ether: RobinLed -- the rear cloud LED as a notification and
 battery indicator

The Robin's rear LED cluster has no AOSP equivalent, so it needs a service of its
own: a NotificationListener that pulses at a rate scaled to how many notifications
are outstanding, and doubles as a battery gauge while charging.

liblight gives the rear cluster up in the same change rather than a later one,
because the point is that there is exactly one writer to leds_on_off. Two writers is
not a worse version of this feature, it is a flickering LED.

The boot chase (led_pattern 4 while bootanim runs) moves from the vendor rc to
init.ether.led.rc on /system. Android 13 init refuses property triggers a vendor rc
is not allowed to see, and init.svc.bootanim is one of them, so the vendor actions
were dropped at parse time and the chase never ran. The write uses the resolved
sysfs path because the /sys/class/leds/.../device link is labelled sysfs_leds and
init cannot read it.
